{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["And Elohim blessed them — in every kind of living creature you find that He blessed them: in fish and birds, in man, and in beast and wild animal." "and fill the waters — imperative mood, and it is of the weak (rife) pattern, like אמרו לאלהים, רדפו מהר. But מַלְּאוּ is imperative, doubled-letter (degesh) pattern, like דַּבְּרוּ אל כל עדת בני ישראל, וְחַזְּקוּ ידים רפות." "י״רב — like יִרְבֶּה and like יִפְנֶה. And so too every verb of the paʿal pattern whose final letter is heh, like פָּנָה, קנה, בנה, מחה, one says וַיִּפֶן, ויקן, ויבן, וימח."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T23:17:23.709957656Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}